{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading","id":1401881,"title":"How worth 1e Corerulebook only for reading","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-09T03:01:54-07:00","id":1401881,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How worth 1e Corerulebook only for reading","content":"To explain it more, in german the only CofD books that are available for VtR are VtR Corerules, Coteries, Lancae Sanctum, Rites of the Dragon, Antagonists, Carthians, Bloodlines: The Hidden and VII. Now I want to ask here, how much worth would it be, to get this limited selection only for reading about the world because I got a little curious how requiem would differ from masquerade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 04-26-2024, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T03:38:22-07:00","id":1401884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading#post1401881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To explain it more, in german the only CofD books that are available are VtR Corerules, Coteries, Antagonists and WtF Corerules. Now I want to ask here, how much worth would it be, to by the corerulebook of the first edition only for reading about the world because I got a little curious how requiem would differ from masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's still worth of as long as you are not considering disciplines, blood sorcery and mechanics.<br /> Another huge change is the mist of ages as well which has been taken out from the 2nd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T04:12:05-07:00","id":1401886,"title":"","content":"It gives you the tone of the game. Also the major clans and covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T05:28:10-07:00","id":1401900,"title":"","content":"Which version of Requiem are you playing? <br /> If you're using mechanics and setting material from 2nd edition, then 1st edition isn't worth it. They aren't the same game in terms of clan, covenant, pseudohistory/origin stories and metaplot. Just labels. If you're looking for additional or different mechanics because you don't like certain features then it may be worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T05:43:24-07:00","id":1401905,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> Oh. They\u2019re that different? I\u2019ve only read some of the 2e stuff in detail, but I flipped thru the 1e corebook once and the clans and covenants looked at least superficially similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T05:49:06-07:00","id":1401907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1401900#post1401900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which version of Requiem are you playing?<br /> If you're using mechanics and setting material from 2nd edition, then 1st edition isn't worth it. They aren't the same game in terms of clan, covenant, pseudohistory/origin stories and metaplot. Just labels. If you're looking for additional or different mechanics because you don't like certain features then it may be worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems you did not read thoroughly or I did not described enough but I do not have any kind of Chronicles of Darkness books. I started with the the World of Darkness with the 20th Anniversary books and now thought of buying the corerolebook of Requiem and Forsaken because those are the only ones that made it for german translation. I do not plan to play them (because the WoD basic Rulebook for this is not available for myself and because I have no other people to play) and only thought about buying it to read it for the fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T06:04:32-07:00","id":1401910,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a> the fluff in VtR 1e is pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T12:54:33-07:00","id":1401948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading#post1401881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To explain it more, in german the only CofD books that are available are VtR Corerules, Coteries, Antagonists and WtF Corerules. Now I want to ask here, how much worth would it be, to by the corerulebook of the first edition only for reading about the world because I got a little curious how requiem would differ from masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I wouldn't recommend it. VTR 1e was the first corebook released for the CofD after ending the WoD, and it shows, with some awkwardness over how willing they were to diverge from Masquerade still. The writing is dry and not super characteristic of how CofD or Requiem ended up becoming in later years, and little elements are misleading, like how the lexicon contains an entry for &quot;caitiff,&quot; an idea which is never returned to in any other Requiem material. You could get about as much value looking up the clans, covenants and Disciplines on wikis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T12:59:25-07:00","id":1401949,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> agreed overall. As far as I can tell, Requiem 2e is far superior to 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T14:09:47-07:00","id":1401964,"title":"","content":"Case by case basis, like Blood the Players Guide for Vampre the Requiem is rules light and a great book for anyone new to VTR2 that did not come from VTR1. Also great for players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T14:23:20-07:00","id":1401967,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of good content for 1e Requiem, but Koronus is looking at an extremely limited set of translated books available, and the VTR 1e corebook alone paints a different picture from VTR with the later supplements that fleshed out the world and further defined its identity as distinct from Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T15:26:11-07:00","id":1401977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1401967#post1401967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's plenty of good content for 1e Requiem, but Koronus is looking at an extremely limited set of translated books available, and the VTR 1e corebook alone paints a different picture from VTR with the later supplements that fleshed out the world and further defined its identity as distinct from Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with some, the state of being a vampire, and how to play a vampire in Blood is amazingly well presented. And if you have a player that has come from say D&amp;D or some such and never before played an undead predator within the twisted Kindred society this guide is very valuable. So each is a case by case based on what you are running, who your players are and how you structure the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T15:40:21-07:00","id":1401979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1401977#post1401977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree with some, the state of being a vampire, and how to play a vampire in Blood is amazingly well presented. And if you have a player that has come from say D&amp;D or some such and never before played an undead predator within the twisted Kindred society this guide is very valuable. So each is a case by case based on what you are running, who your players are and how you structure the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean Blood and Smoke the second edition corerulebook then this advice is at the wrong thread. I asked clearly about the first edition crb because sadly only this got translated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T15:43:22-07:00","id":1401980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1401977#post1401977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with some, the state of being a vampire, and how to play a vampire in Blood is amazingly well presented. And if you have a player that has come from say D&amp;D or some such and never before played an undead predator within the twisted Kindred society this guide is very valuable. So each is a case by case based on what you are running, who your players are and how you structure the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, not one of the books available to OP.<br /> <br /> I also agree that VtR 1e core isn't fully representative of how first edition developed later, and not of second edition, but if you only want to compare the changes between VtM and VtR, it should suffice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T16:05:02-07:00","id":1401983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1401977#post1401977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree with some, the state of being a vampire, and how to play a vampire in Blood is amazingly well presented. And if you have a player that has come from say D&amp;D or some such and never before played an undead predator within the twisted Kindred society this guide is very valuable. So each is a case by case based on what you are running, who your players are and how you structure the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be more relevant if The Blood were in the list of books translated into German available to Koronus. But it isn't, so suggesting it doesn't seem helpful. The only Vampire supplement listed was Coteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 07-09-2020, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T17:42:15-07:00","id":1401995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading#post1401881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To explain it more, in german the only CofD books that are available are VtR Corerules, Coteries, Antagonists and WtF Corerules. Now I want to ask here, how much worth would it be, to by the corerulebook of the first edition only for reading about the world because I got a little curious how requiem would differ from masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies the when I read I thought your intent was to expand beyond what was available in German.<br /> <br /> And Stupid Loserman helped clarify for me.<br /> <br /> I also found this Lancae Sanctum in German on Amazon <br /> <br /> Ein Quellenband Fu\u0308r Vampire: Requiem <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/3937255508/ref=cm_sw_r_other_apa_i_WQ6bFbA0CPYTY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/3937255508/ref=cm_sw_r_other_apa_i_WQ6bFbA0CPYTY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/3937255508/ref=cm_sw_r_other_apa_i_WQ6bFbA0CPYTY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/dp/3937255508/ref=cm_sw_r_other_apa_i_WQ6bFbA0CPYTY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Great read if your drink their koolaid.<br /> <br /> Good luck with the hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T01:13:37-07:00","id":1402023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1401995#post1401995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apologies the when I read I thought your intent was to expand beyond what was available in German.<br /> <br /> And Stupid Loserman helped clarify for me.<br /> <br /> I also found this Lancae Sanctum in German on Amazon <br /> <br /> Ein Quellenband Fu\u0308r Vampire: Requiem <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/3937255508/ref=cm_sw_r_other_apa_i_WQ6bFbA0CPYTY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/3937255508/ref=cm_sw_r_other_apa_i_WQ6bFbA0CPYTY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/3937255508/ref=cm_sw_r_other_apa_i_WQ6bFbA0CPYTY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/dp/3937255508/ref=cm_sw_r_other_apa_i_WQ6bFbA0CPYTY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Great read if your drink their koolaid.<br /> <br /> Good luck with the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome thank you. Sadly back then there whas only lists of english originals but nothing about what made it to german.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T05:16:01-07:00","id":1403372,"title":"","content":"VtR Corerules, Coteries and Antagonists are good reads. I would recommend reading them even if you\u2019re running 2e.<br /> Lancae Sanctum is better than not having it but ideally you want information about all the Covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T11:24:13-07:00","id":1447010,"title":"","content":"Small update. Rites of the Dragon where translated back then too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T22:33:44-07:00","id":1534749,"title":"","content":"Another update. Someone pointed out to me, that Bloodlines: The Hidden, Carthians and VII also made it to German back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 04-26-2024, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T19:41:28-07:00","id":1535242,"title":"","content":"I like the book VII; it was interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T12:30:24-07:00","id":1535523,"title":"","content":"Of the first edition books that I enjoyed were The Invictus, Circle of The Crone and Ordo Dracul and the factions and some of the bloodlines that were put there and helped sell the setting. So yes they are indeed worth the read along with first edition Mage The Awakening and Changeling The Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-13T13:31:10-07:00","id":1535525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1535523#post1535523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of the first edition books that I enjoyed were The Invictus, Circle of The Crone and Ordo Dracul and the factions and some of the bloodlines that were put there and helped sell the setting. So yes they are indeed worth the read along with first edition Mage The Awakening and Changeling The Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Koronus is limited to whatever was released in German, not everything from 1st Ed.<br /> <br /> To be honest, my first great leap in learning English was reading RPG books, so I think that if by now Koronus is sold on the game, it is worth to give it a try to 2nd Edition core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T06:32:55-07:00","id":1535640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1535525#post1535525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Koronus is limited to whatever was released in German, not everything from 1st Ed.<br /> <br /> To be honest, my first great leap in learning English was reading RPG books, so I think that if by now Koronus is sold on the game, it is worth to give it a try to 2nd Edition core.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still kills me that only the Lancea Sanctum book was translated in French, from the old Covenant books. Sure, I can track the other fours in english and in physical copies but the price are a little high for me, and frankly it isn't as comfortable to read all of it in English compared to my native language.<br /> <br /> Damn you, French publishers of back then !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T15:15:36-07:00","id":1535868,"title":"","content":"Unpopular opinion but I prefer 1e to 2e, both in setting and mechanics. And on top of that, I prefer the earlier stuff in VTR 1e that came out before Requiem For Rome and the clanbooks.<br /> <br /> I'd say the selection of VTR 1e books are good and if you can get them, go for it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T16:45:36-07:00","id":1535874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1401881-how-worth-1e-corerulebook-only-for-reading?p=1535868#post1535868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unpopular opinion but I prefer 1e to 2e, both in setting and mechanics. And on top of that, I prefer the earlier stuff in VTR 1e that came out before Requiem For Rome and the clanbooks.<br /> <br /> I'd say the selection of VTR 1e books are good and if you can get them, go for it</div> </div> </div> </div>I do miss the Sleep of Ages as a setting conceit since it made for a major difference between Requiem &amp; Masquerade kindred from the get go and also served as a springboard of sorts for a lot of homebrew weirdness (partly inspired by Awakenning's Astral Realms book) and lore.<br /> <br /> Truth be told, i have a hard time thinking of 1e and 2e as separate things, at least from the setting perspective, due to how much of 2e's (sparse) lore has quite deep roots in 1e concepts from around the time the Clanbooks came out anyway. I suspect i might feel that difference more pointedly if tinkering with the Coil and Scale mechanics of 2e OD, but i have had so little opportunity to play or ST Requiem that who knows when i might have a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-18-2024, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T18:38:12-07:00","id":1535881,"title":"","content":"I can't say I exactly miss 1e core Requiem, but the Sleep of Ages really is a concept that should have stayed. It doesn't just made for a good distinction between the games, it was a really rich concept in how many ways it could be used, be it for story ideas or even for PC creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T16:38:15-07:00","id":1535936,"title":"","content":"Honestly I so far what I read from VTR1 did not convince me. But I have to agree that Sleep of Ages whas really the GOAT. The feature whas so awesome that a friend of mine took it for his own RPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T18:26:53-07:00","id":1535951,"title":"","content":"I hope you someday have an opportunity to read VtR 2e, it isn't as shy from being its own thing. And while it isn't in the 2e book, the Sleep of Ages can be inserted without any big problem.<br /> <br /> But for now, at least you have this piece of a really cool concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T18:27:14-07:00","id":1535952,"title":"","content":"Small reminder that &quot;the sleep of ages&quot; is just torpor and the Fog of Eternity is still there as a thing that can happen often enough for it to serve the same narrative function; &quot;the time you spend dead may result in your memories degrading&quot; being an established known fact in the setting means doesn't need to happen consistently for it to cast doubt on vampires' historical accounts even if they didn't occupy a society of liars with access to supernatural gaslighting techniques and bogeymen who will sabotage their tethers to the living world for a laugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T11:42:38-07:00","id":1536072,"title":"","content":"I always liked Sleep of Ages and how it could mess up a elder or ancients recollection of events as there fears and desires melded to create more dangerous kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}